{"task_id": "Mbpp/61", "solution": "import collections\n\ndef count_Substrings(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of substrings where the sum of digits equals the substring length.\n    This is achieved by transforming each digit d to (d - 1) and counting zero-sum subarrays.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return 0\n\n    # Transform each digit d to (d - 1)\n    transformed_arr = [int(char) - 1 for char in s]\n\n    # Count zero-sum subarrays using prefix sums and a hashmap\n    prefix_sum_counts = collections.defaultdict(int)\n    prefix_sum_counts[0] = 1  # For subarrays starting from index 0 that sum to 0\n    \n    current_sum = 0\n    count = 0\n    for num in transformed_arr:\n        current_sum += num\n        # If current_sum has been seen before, it means the sum of elements\n        # between the previous occurrence and current index is 0.\n        count += prefix_sum_counts[current_sum]\n        prefix_sum_counts[current_sum] += 1\n        \n    return count"}
